 "method": "Proposition prop:be-family compares utilities (accurate results per second). A drone also pays in joules. Per frame,\nabove the board's idle power and with the Pi's measured constants (hardware/energy/energy_constants.json, pi):\n  image q   E_q(B) = e_enc(q) + (a + b B) * 8 b_q / B           encode, then the radio for b_q bytes at goodput B\n  split k   E_k(B) = e_c(k)   + (a + b B) * 8 b_k / B           onboard layers 0..k and the encoder, then the radio\nwith radio power a + b B (W, B in Mbit/s; energy_profile.py's fit), e_c(k) = (s640 inference energy) x (k's edge\nfraction of the network's MACs, the convention of the onboard time) + the quantise + zstd time x the inference power,\nand e_enc(q) the measured 640-pixel JPEG encode energy (the larger of the two measured qualities, 0.0069 J). At the\naccuracy-matched setting q* of Proposition prop:be-family (P A_q >= A_k), with S = 8 (b_q* - b_k) / 1e6 Mbit saved,\nthe split uses less energy per frame iff\n    B < B_E(k) = a S / (e_c(k) - e_enc - b S)        (always, if the denominator is <= 0).\nExact in the model; no fit beyond the measured constants. Also against the JPEG-tuned detector (best of both).\nusage: energy_break_even.py      -> experiments/results/break_even/energy_be.json, energy_be_metrics.tex\n",
